/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A voltage link is simplest.
   - A current link avoids both.
   - Two wires carry supply and signal.
   - The 4 mA start is a live zero.
   - The receiver puts a precision sense resistor in the loop and measures its voltage.
   - Vsense is the sense-resistor voltage in volts; I is loop current in amperes; Rsense is the sense resistance in ohms.
   - Rloop,max is total cable plus resistor resistance in ohms; Vsupply is supply voltage in volts; Vmin is minimum voltage the transmitter needs, about 10 V to 12 V.
   - Use screened twisted pair.
   - Lead resistance matters for resistance sensors, as the second worked example shows.
   - Digital links carry the value as a number.
*/
