/* book exam traps: Pressure in bar is gauge pressure. Use gauge pressure in F = pA; add atmospheric pressure only when a problem asks for absolute pressure. | On the rod side the rod removes area, so retraction force is smaller than extension force at the same pressure. | A 5/2 valve has five ports and two positions, not five positions. The solenoid shifts the spool; it does not set the force. | Pneumatic speed is set by flow control, not by the pressure regulator. Pressure sets force; flow sets speed. | A hydraulic relief valve sets maximum pressure; it does not set flow or direction. */
